Two switches in a row load into the same hidden element, as when VNAS says something (the pet
speaks with an animation) and asks for an animation right after. dsh-pet's second switch took
the element's next loadeddata as its own, and that could be the first clip's: the speaking clip
went in front as if it were the animation, its end answered the animation's command "ended",
and the animation itself, arriving after, was dropped. A switch now waits for the clip it put
in the element.

